<PageTitle>Check retry-created duplicates — Retry Assurance</PageTitle>
<section class="opening"><h1>Does a retry create duplicate jobs?</h1><p class="lede">Run your .NET client against a delayed response, then see how many test jobs it created.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="projects/new">Set up a check</a><a class="button" href="runner">Try the examples</a></div><p class="quiet">Use test data only. Your client runs on your computer or in your build.</p></section>
<section class="flow-strip" aria-label="How it works"><div><b>1</b><h2>Set the expected result</h2><p>Choose which final client outcomes are acceptable.</p></div><div><b>2</b><h2>Run your client</h2><p>The test creates a job, then delays its first reply for three seconds.</p></div><div><b>3</b><h2>Inspect the result</h2><p>See whether the retry reused that job or created another.</p></div></section>
<details><summary>What this check covers</summary><p>The current scenario accepts a JSON POST to jobs. Your client must accept the supplied HttpClient and retry after a timeout. It checks duplicate creation in this scenario, not every possible failure.</p><a href="packs">Scenario details</a></details>
